snd-hda-codec-cs8409 with Apple MacBookPro13,1 support, as a DKMS package.

The driver is the in-tree sound/hda/codecs/cirrus/cs8409 of Linux 7.2 plus the
three patches of the RFC series (../upstream/series-rfc-v1).
hda/ mirrors sound/hda: the three driver files and the private headers they
include. Those headers are the ones of Linux 7.2, so dkms.conf refuses to build
for any other kernel series; for a new series the headers have to be refreshed
from that kernel's source first.

  sudo ./install.sh        take snd_hda_macbookpro out of DKMS, put this in
  sudo reboot              the installed module takes over at the next boot

PACKAGE_VERSION carries the date and the revision of the driver sources it was
exported from.
